    "summary": "Adds a new Go service (services/copilot-review-mcp) that acts as an OAuth 2.0 facade in front of GitHub: RFC 8414 discovery, /authorize redirect, /callback code exchange, /token with S256 PKCE, an in-memory session/code/token-cache store with a janitor goroutine, a bearer-token validation middleware, and docker-compose wiring. The core review surface is the security of the authorization-code flow and the lifecycle of the unbounded in-memory maps. Reviewers should focus on whether PKCE is really enforced, what error details are exposed to clients, and how the store behaves under unauthenticated load.",
    "risk_level": "low",
    "rule_findings": [],
    "suggestions": [
      {
        "file_path": "services/copilot-review-mcp/internal/auth/handler.go",
        "line": 196,
        "severity": "low",
        "confidence": 0.65,
        "title": "Internal error text is returned to clients in the invalid_grant description",
        "reason": "The Token handler passes the raw store error into the OAuth error description (`oauthError(w, \"invalid_grant\", err.Error(), http.StatusBadRequest)`). ExchangeCode in session.go produces distinct internal messages such as `fmt.Errorf(\"redirect_uri mismatch\")` and `fmt.Errorf(\"code not found or expired\")`, and verifyPKCE emits `fmt.Errorf(\"PKCE verification failed\")` / `fmt.Errorf(\"invalid_grant\")`. These are leaked verbatim to unauthenticated callers of POST /token.",
        "recommendation": "Keep the detailed reason server-side and return a stable public description: `slog.Warn(\"token exchange rejected\", \"err\", err)` then `oauthError(w, \"invalid_grant\", \"invalid_grant\", http.StatusBadRequest)`. Alternatively define typed errors in session.go and map them to fixed, non-informative descriptions.",
        "source": "ai",
        "evidence": [
          "oauthError(w, \"invalid_grant\", err.Error(), http.StatusBadRequest)"
        ],
        "failure_scenario": "An attacker probing POST /token with guessed codes and redirect_uri values can distinguish 'code not found or expired' from 'redirect_uri mismatch' from 'PKCE verification failed', which reveals whether a code exists, whether it is still live, and which validation step failed, aiding targeted guessing or reconnaissance."
      }
    ],
